# lock: --python-platform x86_64-manylinux_2_28 --index-strategy unsafe-best-match
# The trainer's tools with the CPU build of PyTorch, for CI's training smoke test and ONNX parity
# check. requirements.txt next to this file is the laptop's GPU set, installed by hand (F-049).
# Locked for Linux amd64 only, which is what CI runs: PyTorch's CPU wheels come from its own
# index, and "best match" lets every other package still come from PyPI. Hashes make that safe.
# Install, then the two local packages:
#   pip install -r requirements-build.txt -r jobs/trainer/requirements-cpu.txt
#   pip install --no-deps --no-build-isolation -e packages/wikiguard_core -e jobs/trainer
--extra-index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu
